<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Nikola Altomanović</h1><p class="st-meta">1366 CE – 1373 CE (approx.) · capital Užice</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Short-lived lordship of the Serbian magnate Nikola Altomanović, the largest in western Serbia after the collapse of Dušan's empire.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikola-altomanovic">Nikola Altomanović</a>, son of a nobleman in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan's</a> service, built up lands in the 1360s as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-uros-v">Uroš V</a>'s authority faded. By about 1371 he held a broad territory from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudnik">Rudnik</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzice">Užice</a> to the borders of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-ragusa">Ragusa</a> and Hum.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nikola ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzice">Užice</a> as an independent lord, taxing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudnik">Rudnik</a> and quarrelling with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-ragusa">Ragusa</a> over trade dues. He was aggressive towards his neighbours, plotting against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lazar-of-serbia">Prince Lazar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tvrtko-i-of-bosnia">Tvrtko</a> I of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/banate-of-bosnia">Banate of Bosnia</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1373 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lazar-of-serbia">Lazar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tvrtko-i-of-bosnia">Tvrtko</a>, backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-i-of-hungary">Louis I of Hungary</a>, defeated him; he was captured at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzice">Užice</a> and blinded. His lands were divided between Lazar's <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/moravian-serbia">Moravian Serbia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durad-i-balsic">Đurađ I Balšić</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeta-region">Zeta</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1366 CE – 1373 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Balkans and Hungary</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:86.89%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1366 CE – 1373 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Užice</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Nikola Altomanović</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Serbian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a>, <a href="/countries/montenegro">Montenegro</a>, <a href="/countries/bosnia-and-herzegovina">Bosnia and Herzegovina</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Altomanović lands</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1370&amp;focus=lordship-of-nikola-altomanovic" aria-label="Lordship of Nikola Altomanović on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5156 624 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Nikola Altomanović lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5476 880L5521 939M5476 880L5513 889"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5521 939h0M5513 889h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5476 880h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5476 880h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Užice. <a href="/atlas?year=1370&amp;focus=lordship-of-nikola-altomanovic">On the atlas &rarr;</a>